# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file every `docker build` and
# every `docker compose up` ships the whole repository as build context — 1,379
# tracked files, most of which the build never reads.
#
# vendor/ is NOT excluded, and must not be: the build is deliberately hermetic
# (`go build -mod=vendor` with no network), which is what lets a stranger build
# offline and what stops a release publishing an unbuildable binary.
.git
docs
docs-site
*.md
